86571229 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571229 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "db423193-4755-5aa1-a9f5-871e3febcb41" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571240 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571240 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571240 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e28a5398-d9ed-502e-977d-28d4a3a660ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571298 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186570966 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571298 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186570992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571298 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571066 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571298 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571298 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571225 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571298 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571298 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571298 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186570992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571298 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "24e8cec7-9fe1-550d-b2c4-3278855ff161" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571301 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186570962 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571301 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571056 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571301 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571098 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571301 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571229 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571301 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571240 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571301 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571301 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571301 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186571056 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571301 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "2c1667ad-3207-5d60-a6a8-63d80d6cb9a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571386 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571298 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571386 #edb/ref 1069 "q-106808" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571386 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571386 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $V$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices with real entries and determinant $0.$ Which of the following statements are true?  \n\nI. The zero-matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ belongs to $V.$\n\nII. Scalar multiplication of matrices in $V$ is associative.\n\nIII. For any $A,B\\in V$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (A+B)=\\alpha A+\\alpha B.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571386 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "34bd5220-616c-5a5a-8d4a-800215bc060f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571386 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}=0.$ Hence, $\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\in V.$\n\n- Statements II is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A=({a}_{ij})\\in V,$ the entries are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha (\\beta {a}_{ij})=(\\alpha \\beta ){a}_{ij},\n$$\n\nand hence,\n\n$$\n\\alpha (\\beta A)=(\\alpha \\beta )A.\n$$\n\n- Statements III is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrices $A=({a}_{ij})$ and $B=({b}_{ij})$ from $V,$ the entries are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha ({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij})=\\alpha {a}_{ij}+\\alpha {b}_{ij},\n$$\n\nand hence,\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )A=\\alpha A+\\beta A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571433 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571433 #edb/ref 1069 "q-106707" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571433 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571433 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $B$ be the set of all functions $f:Q\\to Q$ such that $f(0)=\\frac{1}{2}.$  Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. For each $f(x)\\in B$, we have $-f(x)\\in B$ such that $f(x)+(-f(x))=0.$\n\nII. For any $f(x),g(x),h(x)\\in B,$ we have $[f(x)-g(x)]+h(x)=f(x)-[g(x)+h(x)].$\n\nIII. The addition of functions in $B$ is commutative." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571433 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a462519c-8f3a-5164-b4fe-0415a57a0df2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571433 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's verify the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, consider a function $f(x)\\in B$ where $f(0)=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Then $-f(x)$ is the corresponding negative function such that\n\n$$\nf(x)+(-f(x))=f(x)-f(x)=0.\n$$\n\nHowever,\n\n$$\n-f(0)=-\\frac{1}{2}\\ne \\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nand, hence, $-f(x)\\notin B.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, consider the functions $f(x)={x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2},$ $g(x)=\\frac{1}{2},$ and $h(x)=2{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2},$ from $B.$ Then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[f(x)-g(x)]+h(x) & =[{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}]+2{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ f(x)-[g(x)+h(x)] & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}-[\\frac{1}{2}+2{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}] \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}-[2{x}^{2}+1] \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}-2{x}^{2}-1 \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $[f(x)-g(x)]+h(x)\\ne f(x)-[g(x)+h(x)].$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any functions $f(x),g(x)\\in B,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\nf(x)+g(x)=g(x)+f(x)\n$$\n\nsince the addition of functions is commutative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
